---
import WalkthroughLayout from '../../layouts/WalkthroughLayout.astro';
import ChapterCard from '../../components/ChapterCard.astro';
import TacticalBriefing from '../../components/TacticalBriefing.astro';
import AsciiMap from '../../components/AsciiMap.astro';
import BossCard from '../../components/BossCard.astro';
import ShopMatrix from '../../components/ShopMatrix.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const quickJumps = [
  { "id": "ch01", "number": 1, "title": "Alistel (Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch02", "number": 2, "title": "Lazvil Hills (Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch03", "number": 3, "title": "Alistel (Alternate Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch04", "number": 4, "title": "Lazvil Hills (Alternate Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch05", "number": 5, "title": "Alma Mine (Alternate Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch06", "number": 6, "title": "Alistel (Standard Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch07", "number": 7, "title": "Alistel (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch08", "number": 8, "title": "Lazvil Hills (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch09", "number": 9, "title": "Judgement Cliff (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch10", "number": 10, "title": "Sand Fortress (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" }
];

const stats = {
  chapters: 10,
  nodes: 14,
  endings: 2,
  sidequests: 5,
  bosses: 4
};

const prevVol = undefined;
const nextVol = { num: 2, title: 'Specint Espionage & Underground Passages', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-2/` };
---

<WalkthroughLayout
  volume={1}
  volumeTitle="Prologue & First Assignments"
  chapterRange="Chapters 01–10"
  description="The fateful choice at Lazvil Hills. Inception of Standard History (Specint) and Alternate History (Rosch Brigade), Sand Fortress infiltration, and first Historia nodes."
  stats={stats}
  quickJumps={quickJumps}
  prevVol={prevVol}
  nextVol={nextVol}
>

  <!-- Chapter 01 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch01"
    number={1}
    title="Alistel (Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="1"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      inn="50 G"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix
        title="Alistel Ward Inventories"
        items={[
          { name: "Soothing Balm", price: 100 },
          { name: "Herbal Tea", price: 350 },
          { name: "Holy Water", price: 500 },
          { name: "Anti-Poison", price: 50 },
          { name: "Poison Wing", price: 350 }
        ]}
        equipment={[
          { name: "Epee", price: 500 },
          { name: "Custom Sword", price: 700, note: "buy for Stocke" },
          { name: "Bronze Spear", price: 1000 },
          { name: "Custom Lance", price: 1600 },
          { name: "Bronze Mail", price: 900 },
          { name: "Beast Skins", price: 500 },
          { name: "Pawn Stud", price: 750 },
          { name: "Seed Ring", price: 1000 }
        ]}
      />

      <AsciiMap title="Alistel Castle & Wards (1F, 2F, 3F)">
<pre>__       __             _____   _ ___
 |  |__E__|  |    3F     | _|  | | |__ |   Second Ward    S - Save Point
 |__  ___  __|           |  _  |S|   _ |                  E - Elevator
   /S/ | \2\             | |  _| |_  | |                  X - Inaccessible
   \/  |  \/             | |___   _ _| |                  1 - Soothing Balm x2
  __   |   __            |__ |_   _|5__|                  2 - Charm
 |  |__E__|  |    2F        X  | |                        3 - Holy Water
 |__  ___  __|                    ____                    4 - Herbal Tea x2
   /1/ | \ \              _____| |___ |_   First Ward     5 - Herbal Tea
   \/  |  \/             |_____   ____  |                 6 - 300 G
  __   |   __             _____| |__7_| |                 7 - Beast Skins
 |  |__E__|34|    1F     |_____   ____| |
 |__       __|X|               | |6_____|
|       S      |               | |
|____     _____|
     |   |
       |
 To Second Ward</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Daydream">
        <p>After receiving your first mission, let&#x27;s promptly ignore it and go treasure hunting first. To your left, you should find a chest which contains 2 SOOTHING BALMS. Take the central elevator up to the third floor and open the chest to the right which contains a CHARM (ATK+1/MAG+1/HP+3, equip on Raynie). Now, head down to the first floor. In the upper right room are two chests which contain a HOLY WATER and 2 HERBAL TEAS.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>In the Second Ward, there is a tavern to the left and the equipment shop to the right. Climb both stairs on the right and run down to a chest which contains an HERBAL TEA. Return to the main corridor and head down to the First Ward.</p>

      <p>Climb the stairs to your right and follow the path around to a chest which contains 300 G. Go back to the corridor. To the left is the item shop and the inn is to the right. Check out the inn&#x27;s second floor where you can find a chest which contains BEAST SKINS (DEF+9/MDF+12, equip on Stocke).</p>

      <p>With the new money you found, return to the equipment shop and purchase a Custom Sword for Stocke. Hand down his old Bronze Sword to Marco and sell your excess equipment. As you leave the city, talk to Rosch, and continue to Lazvil Hills.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Custom Sword, Beast Skins<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Spear, Brigandine, Charm<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Bronze Sword, Brigandine</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 02 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch02"
    number={2}
    title="Lazvil Hills (Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="1"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      enemies={[
        { name: "Dodo", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Light Granorgite" }
      ]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Children of Historia">
        <p>Your first expedition outside Alistel leads directly into the fog of Lazvil Hills.</p>
      </Callout>

      <AsciiMap title="Lazvil Hills - Highway W & Woodland Path">
<pre>                   Highway W    Highway
                                  ___
                  ___________   _/C  \_     S - Save Point
                 X_____    __   _     _     X - Inaccessible
                 | 3 _____/      \___/      C - Chest you can&#x27;t get yet
                  \  __|                    1 - Soothing Balm x3
Woodland          | |                       2 - Royal Jelly x3
 Path W                                     3 - Bronze Mail*
   _____   _______| |                           *Requires super strength
 _|  S _   _   _   _|
|     |     \1/ | |    Woodland
|      X       /   \_    Path
 \_   /       /   S X
   |X|       /2_____X</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p>Immediately upon your arrival, you are thrown into some tutorial battles. The instruction manual and in-game tutorials go over this well enough, so I don&#x27;t feel the need to do so again. When you regain control of Stocke, head east to the Woodland Path. Below you, is a chest which contains 3 SOOTHING BALMS. Continue east to another scene.</p>

      <p>Once again, promptly ignore where you are told to go, and head down to a chest which contains 3 ROYAL JELLIES. Now, head north and complete another tutorial battle. Proceed north to Highway West and you will gain the Strike ability. Use it to stun enemies on the field, so you can gain a preemptive strike. Remember the crates in the cave you just passed for later and proceed east to the Highway. You cannot reach the chest behind the brush above, so cross the bridge to the east.</p>

      <BossCard
        name="Palomides, Granorg Archer x3"
        weakness="HA!"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> None. This is a scripted battle that you cannot win. Stocke might as well have just stayed in bed this morning.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>After some events, you will meet Lippti and Teo of Historia. When you regain control of Stocke, first head south to the blockade. Lippti and Teo will appear again to give you superhuman strength to move them. Again, ignore the blockade and head north to the Highway West. Enter the cave and move the crates to gain access to a chest which contains a BRONZE MAIL (DEF+14/MDF+10, equip on Marco). Return to the blockade, follow the path to another battle, and you will make it out alive this time.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Awakening">
        <p>Upon awakening back at Alistel, leave the infirmary and try to leave to the right. Afterwards, you will be given a critical decision to make.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Beginning">
        <p>Head upstairs and talk to Rosch. Now, you have a decision to make: to Join the Rosch Brigade or to Stay under Heiss. This is where the main timeline will split into Standard History (SH) by staying under Heiss and Alternate History (AH) by joining the Rosch Brigade. Eventually, you will need to use the White Chronicle to take both paths, so don&#x27;t worry about which path to take first. You&#x27;re not going to be locked out of anything. I would recommend joining the Rosch Brigade first, since it unlocks some sidequests. If you wish to proceed by staying under Heiss, then skip ahead to Chapter 06 (Alistel - Standard Prologue).</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Custom Sword, Beast Skins<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Spear, Brigandine, Charm<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Bronze Sword, Bronze Mail</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 03 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch03"
    number={3}
    title="Alistel (Alternate Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="4"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Joining Rosch Brigade">
        <p>After talking with Rosch, Raul, and Kiel, Rosch will join your party. Since you can only use three party members at a time, use the Party command in the menu screen to switch in Rosch for Marco. This will leave you with a mage to use, while keeping Marco&#x27;s MP up for healing outside of battle. Also, give Marco&#x27;s Bronze Mail to Raynie, while he is inactive. You should also switch Raynie&#x27;s stronger Spear with Rosch&#x27;s Light Lance, since he&#x27;ll be using physical attacks far more often.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Before heading to your next mission, you can pick up your first sidequests now. Take the elevator down to the first floor and talk to the receptionist behind the desk to the left to receive the [Soldier Recruit] sidequest. Head down to the First Ward and talk to the soldier on the left to receive the [Night Watch] sidequest. You will eventually need to buy two Anti-Sleeps for him, but they&#x27;re not available right now.</p>

      <p>Check out the inn and talk to the two mercenaries there to advance the [Soldier Recruit] sidequest. Return to the receptionist to complete it and receive 1500 G for your reward. Instead of upgrading your equipment here, I would save it for now, as better equipment will become available in the very near future. Leave Alistel and head for Lazvil Hills again.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Custom Sword, Beast Skins<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Light Lance, Bronze Mail, Charm<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Bronze Sword, Brigandine<br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> Spear, Brigandine</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 04 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch04"
    number={4}
    title="Lazvil Hills (Alternate Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="4"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Rosch"
      enemies={[
        { name: "Bush Lizard", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Dodo", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Killer Bee", weakness: "Fire" }
      ]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix
        title="Traveling Merchant Inventory"
        items={[
          { name: "Soothing Balm", price: 100 },
          { name: "First Aid Kit", price: 400 },
          { name: "Herbal Tea", price: 350 },
          { name: "Holy Water", price: 500 },
          { name: "Anti-Poison", price: 50 },
          { name: "Poison Wing", price: 350 },
          { name: "Sleep Wing", price: 500 }
        ]}
        itemTitle="Provisions"
      />

      <AsciiMap title="Lazvil Hills - Broken Bridge & Detour Map">
<pre>                Highway W               Highway         Highway E

                                    ___                     | |
           __________________   ___/C  \_ ____________   __/   \
           ____________    __   ___     _X ______   __   _      |
                 |   _____/        \___/  |    ____/      |     |
                  \  __|           |Z  |   \  |            \   /
Woodland          | |               \  |    | |             |X|
 Path W           | |                | |    | |             | |

   _____   _______| |               _| |    | |
 _|  S _   _   _   _|              |_X |   /  |  Woodland
|     |     \_/ | |    Woodland      | |__|   |   Path E
|      X       /   \____ Path        |_   ____|
 \_   /       /   S     \____   _______| |
   |X|       /_______________   _________|

S - Save Point   X - Inaccessible   Z - Cave-in   C - Chest you can&#x27;t get yet</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p>This time, the trip through Lazvil Hills is uneventful. There are two points of interest. First, the bridge is out, so you&#x27;ll have to take the long way around. Second, there is a cave under the bridge where a soldier is trapped by a cave-in. There&#x27;s nothing we can do to help him out for now, but remember that for later.</p>

      <p>The path to Alma Mine is fairly straight-forward. Head west, take the lower path south and west to the Woodland Path. Then, go north at the fork and west to the exit.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 05 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch05"
    number={5}
    title="Alma Mine (Alternate Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="6"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Rosch"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix
        title="Alma Mine Traveling Merchant"
        items={[
          { name: "Soothing Balm", price: 100 },
          { name: "Herbal Tea", price: 350 },
          { name: "Holy Water", price: 500 },
          { name: "Anti-Poison", price: 50 },
          { name: "Poison Wing", price: 350 }
        ]}
        equipment={[
          { name: "Custom Sword", price: 700 },
          { name: "Silver Edge", price: 3000 },
          { name: "Custom Lance", price: 1600 },
          { name: "Iron Spear", price: 1800 },
          { name: "Bronze Mail", price: 900 },
          { name: "Silver Cape", price: 2800 },
          { name: "Charm", price: 350 },
          { name: "Horn Charm", price: 1000, note: "buy 3 for Raynie" },
          { name: "Pawn Stud", price: 750 },
          { name: "Seed Ring", price: 1000 }
        ]}
      />

      <AsciiMap title="Alma Mine - Material Storage Area">
<pre> Material
 Storage

  _ |X|_     S - Save Point
 /2/   S\    X - Inaccessible
| |_     |   1 - Soothing Balm x3
| |1|    |   2 - 200 G
|        |
 \__   _/
    | |</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p>Upon arriving at Alma Mine, you have your second decision to make. This time, there is a right and wrong answer. If you want to unlock every node in the game, you will want to choose the wrong answer, as this unlocks bad endings throughout the game. Choosing to &quot;Wait in ambush&quot; will unlock [The Fallen Capital] ending. Otherwise, choosing to &quot;Send scouts&quot; will prompt a roadblock in the story that can only be overcome in the other timeline.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Closed Mine">
        <p>If you chose to wait in ambush, then you will be sent back to the beginning of the chapter, so press Start to skip the cutscene. Fortunately, since this was a critical decision point, a travel node has been created, so you can just skip back to that decision. At a save point, choose &quot;Go to Historia&quot;, return to &quot;The Closed Mine&quot; node, and choose to &quot;Send Scouts&quot;. While you won&#x27;t get a bad ending this time, the plot cannot proceed on this timeline for now. If you have already resolved this roadblock, then skip ahead to Chapter 12 (Alma Mine - Alternate Prologue).</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Breaking Rocks">
        <p>Before checking out the other timeline, there&#x27;s still things you can do here. Walk down to find a merchant outside of a house. Buy 3 Horn Charms for Raynie to receive a good boost to her Magic stat that will last a very long time. I would recommend saving your remaining funds for better purchases later. Inside the house is a chest which contains 3 SOOTHING BALMS. Go up the ramp to the left to find a chest which contains 200 G.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Since you are unable to continue further, use Historia to return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node. This time, talk to Rosch and tell him you are choosing to &quot;Stay under Heiss&quot;.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 06 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch06"
    number={6}
    title="Alistel (Standard Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="6"
      party="Stocke"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <p>Take the elevator up to the second floor where you will receive your next mission from Heiss.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Specint Assignment">
        <p>Go back down the elevator and south to the item shop in the First Ward. Talk to the item shop owner to learn that you need to head to the tavern to find your target. Head back up to the Second Ward, enter the bar, and watch the scene. When the robed man leaves, follow him, and confront him.</p>
      </Callout>

      <BossCard
        name="Vlad"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> If you have learned Power Wave, use it. Otherwise, stick to your normal attacks, and cast Heal when your HP falls below 50.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>After defeating Vlad, return to Heiss&#x27; office to receive your next mission.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Top Secret Mission">
        <p>Head down to the first floor, and you will begin the first chapter.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 07 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch07"
    number={7}
    title="Alistel (Standard Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="6"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: To Granorg">
        <p>You need to find Raynie and Marco, who can be found at the tavern.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Bridge at Lazvil">
        <p>Shops will periodically sell new equipment from chapter to chapter, but not this time. Before heading to Lazvil again, let&#x27;s pick up some sidequests. Climb the stairs to the left of the tavern and talk to the girl, named Anna. Listen to her requests and accept [The King&#x27;s Daughter] sidequest from her.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Go right to the weapon shop and talk to the kids to the right. Listen to their problem and accept the [What Was Inherited] sidequest. Climb the stairs and enter the upper right house. Talk to the kids&#x27; father to advance [What Was Inherited]. Rest up at the inn and head to Lazvil Hills.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Custom Sword, Beast Skins, Charm<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Light Lance, Brigandine, Horn Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Bronze Sword, Bronze Mail</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 08 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch08"
    number={8}
    title="Lazvil Hills (Standard Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="6"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      enemies={[
        { name: "Blue Flame", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Feepo", weakness: "Lightning" },
        { name: "Flame Lizard", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Venom Bee", weakness: "Fire" }
      ]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap title="Lazvil Hills - Detailed Tactical Map">
<pre>                Highway W               Highway         Highway E

                                    ___                     | |
           __________________   ___/C  \_ ____________   __/   \
          X____________    __   ___     _X ______   __   _      |
                 |   _____/        \___/  |    ____/      |     |
                  \  __|           |2  |   \  |            \   /
Woodland          | |               \  |    | |             |X|
 Path W           | |                | |    | |             | |

   _____   _______| |               _| |    | |            _| |_
