      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Breakthrough">
        <p>There is no treasure to be found here for now, so it&#x27;s very straight-forward. In the Sand Fortress South area, hug the west cliffs to avoid stepping on any traps on the main road. Before entering the fortress, you will also find a merchant. I would recommend buying 6 Fang Charms, giving 3 of each to Stocke and Marco. A Rune Spear will greatly boost Raynie&#x27;s magic stat. All of these will last you for a very long time. However, I&#x27;d save the remaining money for buying armor later. You can also buy 2 Anti-Sleeps for the [Night Watch] sidequest, which we&#x27;ll be completing soon enough. If you can afford it, I would also purchase a Rune Edge for Stocke. Maybe try buying it after looting some of the soldiers. Hand down his old Custom Sword to Marco.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>The path through the Sand Fortress can be very short. If you just walk right up the middle staircases, you can make it up to the third floor without a fight. Then, walk around to the right and up the stairs to the exit. However, I&#x27;d strongly recommend fighting every soldier that you can, just for the gold and experience. Plus, you still might pick up a Vital Blade from the Feepos around here too. When you&#x27;re ready, go through the door atop the third floor for your last trial.</p>

      <BossCard
        name="Granorg Defender, Granorg Archer x2, Light Granorgite x2"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Marco should cast Magic Boost on Raynie and Stocke, while they use Push Assault and Thunder to take out a Light Granorgite and Granorg Archer. Once they&#x27;re all out of the way, I would use the Change command to string together six consecutive turns of alternating between physical attacks and spells to finish off the Granorg Defender.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>For defeating them, you will gain access to the Sand Fortress North area. The exit can be found to the northeast. Before continuing on to the Gran Plain, you should rest up back at Alistel.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
